                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">Hand of the Emperor</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, add 1 to Advance rolls and charge rolls made for ADEPTUS SORORITAS units from your army.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="-2-" id="2ee2-27e3-2614-956b" hidden="false" typeId="9274-72c0-35b3-10df" typeName="Roll">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">Spirit of the Martyr</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, each time an ADEPTUS SORORITAS model from your army is destroyed by a melee attack and does not explode, roll one D6: on a 6, after the attacking model’s unit has finished making its attacks, it suffers 1 mortal wound.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="-3-" id="b861-7627-0598-7b33" hidden="false" typeId="9274-72c0-35b3-10df" typeName="Roll">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">Aegis of the Emperor</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, each time a unit form your army uses its Shield of Faith ability to take a Deny the Witch test, if the result of that test was an unmodified result of 5+, or if it was greater than the result of the Psychic test, that Deny the Witch test is passed.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="-4-" id="1cac-e085-af4d-6aee" hidden="false" typeId="9274-72c0-35b3-10df" typeName="Roll">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">Divine Guidance</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, each time an ADEPTUS SORORITAS model from your army makes a ranged attack, on an unmodified wound roll of 6, the Damage characteristic of that attack is improved by 1.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="-5-" id="18c1-4d5f-98d5-7a63" hidden="false" typeId="9274-72c0-35b3-10df" typeName="Roll">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">The Passion</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, each time an ADEPTUS SORORITAS model from your army makes a melee attack, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="-6-" id="3f3d-369e-6b19-a908" hidden="false" typeId="9274-72c0-35b3-10df" typeName="Roll">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Sacred Rite" typeId="0b60-5047-23a0-c7b2">Light of the Emperor</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="19b7-7dce-abef-5f9a">While this sacred rite is active, you can ignore any or all modifiers to the Leadership characteristic of ADEPTUS SORORITAS units from your army, and each time a Combat Attrition test is taken for that unit, you can ignore any or all modifiers.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </infoGroup>
          </infoGroups>
          <profiles>
            <profile name=" Acts of Faith - Gaining Miracle Dice" id="4f6f-6e41-a05a-30d6" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Gaining Miracle Dice:
 - At the start of each turn, you gain 1 Miracle dice.
 - At the end of a phase, when any ADEPTUS SORORITAS destroy one or more enemy units.
 - At the end of a phase, when one or more ADEPTUS SORORITAS CHARACTER units from your army are destroyed.

Each time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side - this is your Miracle dice pool.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name=" Acts of Faith" id="e857-efd6-4722-1eb3" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">- Once per phase, one ADEPTUS SORORITAS unit from your army can perform one Act of Faith. To do so, you will use Miracle dice.
- Before making a dice roll for a ADEPTUS SORORITAS model or a unit from your army, you can select one or more of the dice from your Miracle dice pool, and, for each individual dice that is being rolled as part of the dice roll, you can select 1 Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool to be substituted in place of that dice.
- The dice that it is being substituted for is not rolled, and instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled.
- Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once, and when used, removed from the Miracle dice pool.
- A Miracle dice that has been used for a substitution can never be re-rolled.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name=" Sacred Rites" id="d9da-79d7-6726-0e58" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">After players have determined their mission, you must select one Sacred rite from the following table to be active for your army.
Alternatively, you can randomly determine two Sacred rites from the table to be active for your army by rolling two D6 and looking up the results.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
      </infoGroups>
